Presets collect output settings so you can reuse a conversion setup. Open the **Presets** inspector tab with a source selected.

## Choose a built-in preset

Frame includes these starting points:

| Preset | Intended use |
| --- | --- |
| Balanced MP4 | General-purpose video conversion. |
| Archive H.265 | An H.265 configuration for archiving video. |
| Web Share | Video prepared for sharing. |
| GIF Web Small | A smaller animated GIF. |
| GIF High Quality | An animated GIF with more detail. |
| Audio MP3 | MP3 audio output. |
| Audio FLAC (Lossless) | Lossless FLAC audio output. |
| Discord | A video configuration for sharing on Discord. |

Preset availability depends on the selected source. A preset that cannot be applied to that media type is disabled.

Names describe the intended use; they do not guarantee a particular file size or compatibility with every service. Check the actual output settings and test the result in its destination.

<DocsScreenshot
  scene="presets"
